---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<div class="wrap">

		<header>
			<div class="header-inner">
				<span class="site-name">Nat Plamondon</span>
				<nav>
					<a href="#work">Work</a>
					<a href="#writing">Writing</a>
					<a href="#contact">Contact</a>
				</nav>
			</div>
		</header>

		<main>

			<section class="hero">
				<h1>Portfolio positioning for companies that outgrew their story.</h1>
				<div class="hero-body">
					<p>Most companies reach a point where the product portfolio has grown faster than the story holding it together. Acquisitions, new product lines, category shifts — the narrative that worked at Series B stops working when you are explaining three products to a skeptical enterprise buyer.</p>
					<p>I build the framework when there isn't one yet. Ten years of platform repositioning, acquisition messaging integration, and the category work that has to hold up across an entire company — not just a launch.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<hr />

			<section id="work">
				<div class="section-header">
					<h2 class="section-label">Work</h2>
					<p class="section-intro">The work I'm best known for is what happens after the easy positioning is gone — when the portfolio is bigger than the original story, the acquisition just closed, or the category has shifted under you. The question is always the same: what do we actually sell now, and how do we make sure everyone from the CEO to the field says it the same way.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="case-list">

					<article class="case">
						<div class="case-meta">
							<span class="tag">Platform Repositioning</span>
						</div>
						<h3>From Learning Suite to Workforce Agility Platform</h3>
						<p>Cornerstone had accumulated a strong product portfolio and a fragmented story. L&D buyers heard the LMS narrative. HR buyers heard the performance narrative. Executive buyers heard nothing coherent. The individual products were defensible; the platform wasn't.</p>
						<p>The work was to find the unifying outcome that every product could honestly claim to serve — and build a messaging architecture from that outcome down to the product level, precise enough that a global sales and marketing team could execute it without drift. The result was a platform narrative anchored in workforce agility: the idea that the most durable competitive advantage is an organization's ability to continuously adapt its people. That repositioning produced a 440% increase in multi-product adoption.</p>
					</article>

					<article class="case">
						<div class="case-meta">
							<span class="tag">Platform Repositioning</span>
						</div>
						<h3>Workforce Readiness: When the Market Shifts Under You</h3>
						<p>Platform narratives have a shelf life. The workforce agility positioning had worked — until the pandemic made "agility" sound abstract at exactly the moment buyers needed concrete answers to concrete problems. The vocabulary had shifted. The positioning had to move with it.</p>
						<p>The second repositioning didn't replace the platform narrative — it sharpened it. Agility became readiness: measurable, operational, tied to business continuity rather than transformation aspiration. The harder problem was making the evolution feel like evolution, not contradiction. Existing customers had bought the first story. The language bridges had to hold across both.</p>
					</article>

					<article class="case">
						<div class="case-meta">
							<span class="tag">M&A Messaging Integration</span>
						</div>
						<h3>Making Two Acquisitions Make Sense: Edcast &amp; SkyHive</h3>
						<p>Cornerstone acquired EdCast and SkyHive in quick succession — an enterprise learning experience platform and an AI-powered skills intelligence engine. Both brought distinct technology, distinct buyers, and distinct market identities. The standard playbook for acquisitions like this is to fold them into the mothership story and hope the details sort themselves out. The result is usually language that makes both companies sound smaller than they were.</p>
						<p>The work was integration without erasure. That meant identifying what each acquisition strengthened in the platform narrative, what needed to change and what needed to stay, and building the specific language bridges that let sales tell a coherent combined story fast enough to support go-to-market momentum through the transition. SkyHive grew approximately 100% year-over-year in its first full year as part of Cornerstone.</p>
					</article>

				</div>
			</section>

			<hr />

			<section id="writing">
				<div class="section-header">
					<h2 class="section-label">Writing</h2>
					<p class="section-intro">Thinking on portfolio positioning, acquisition messaging, and the problems in product marketing that don't get talked about enough.</p>
				</div>

				<ul class="writing-list">
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nathanielplamondon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="writing-item">
							<span class="writing-title">LinkedIn</span>
							<span class="writing-desc">Posts on positioning, PMM craft, and enterprise SaaS — the ongoing conversation.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
					<li class="writing-item writing-item--soon">
						<span class="writing-title">Substack <span class="soon-badge">Coming soon</span></span>
						<span class="writing-desc">Longer-form writing on portfolio positioning, M&A messaging, and the overlooked problems in product marketing.</span>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<hr />

			<section id="contact">
				<div class="section-header">
					<h2 class="section-label">Contact</h2>
				</div>
				<p>For conversations about positioning, platform narratives, or what it takes to make a complicated product story land — <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nathanielplamondon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> is the right place to start.</p>
			</section>

		</main>

		<footer>
			<div class="footer-inner">
				<span>Nat Plamondon</span>
				<span>{new Date().getFullYear()}</span>
			</div>
		</footer>

	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* Layout */
	.wrap {
		box-sizing: border-box;
		max-width: 780px;
		margin-right: auto;
		margin-left: auto;
		padding: 0 2rem;
	}

	/* Header */
	header {
		background: var(--bg);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		padding: 1.25rem 0;
	}

	.header-inner {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
	}

	.site-name {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 15px;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--text);
		letter-spacing: 0;
	}

	nav {
		display: flex;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	nav a {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 11px;
		font-weight: 400;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.15s;
	}

	nav a:hover {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	/* Hero */
	.hero {
		padding: 8rem 0 5rem;
	}

	h1 {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 2.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.15;
		color: var(--text);
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.hero-body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 560px;
	}

	.hero-body p {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 17px;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.hero-body strong {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	/* Dividers */
	hr {
		border: none;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	/* Sections */
	section {
		padding: 5rem 0;
	}

	.section-header {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.section-label {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 13px;
		font-weight: 400;
		font-style: italic;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.section-intro {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 17px;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		max-width: 540px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	/* Case studies */
	.case-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.case {
		background: var(--bg-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.case-meta {
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}

	.tag {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 10px;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--accent-secondary);
	}

	.case h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.3;
		color: var(--text);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.case p {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 14.5px;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.75;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	.case p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	/* Writing */
	.writing-list {
		list-style: none;
	}

	.writing-item {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		padding: 1.25rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
		text-decoration: none;
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.writing-list li:first-child > .writing-item,
	.writing-list li:first-child.writing-item {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	a.writing-item .writing-title {
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	a.writing-item:hover .writing-title {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
	}

	.writing-item--soon {
		opacity: 0.5;
	}

	.writing-title {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--text);
		transition: color 0.15s;
	}

	.writing-desc {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 14px;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.soon-badge {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 9px;
		font-weight: 400;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
		border-radius: 2px;
	}

	/* Contact */
	#contact p {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.8;
		max-width: 480px;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	#contact a {
		color: var(--accent);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	#contact a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}

	/* Footer */
	footer {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		padding: 1.75rem 0;
	}

	.footer-inner {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	footer span {
		font-family: var(--font-ui);
		font-size: 11px;
		font-weight: 400;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	/* Mobile */
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.wrap {
			padding: 0 1.25rem;
		}

		.hero {
			padding: 5rem 0 3.5rem;
		}

		section {
			padding: 3.5rem 0;
		}

		.case {
			padding: 1.25rem;
		}

		nav {
			gap: 1.25rem;
		}
	}
</style>
